/**
 * The metrics Core\Pdf needs to lay out text in the standard PDF fonts (3.40) – Helvetica and Times in regular and bold;
 * Courier is 600 wide for every character. PDF readers carry these fonts, so nothing is embedded.
 *
 * The characters are ASCII, Latin-1, the extra punctuation of Windows-1252 (– — “ ” „ … € ™), the Central and Eastern
 * European letters of Latin Extended-A that the core-14 fonts draw (č ě ř š ž ů ő ł ą ę ğ ş ı ș ț …) and a few signs
 * (− ≤ ≥ ≠). Anything else (Greek, Cyrillic, Arabic, Chinese, Vietnamese tones) is not drawable – Core\Pdf::supports().
 * The widths are the metric-compatible values (Arial for Helvetica, Times New Roman for Times), in thousandths of the size.
 */
